## KanjiVG — stroke-order data

A 6,703-character normalized KanjiVG-derived pack is distributed in
`api/storage/strokes/` and served at `GET /content/strokes/:codepoint`. The
current curriculum guarantees coverage for its 336 taught characters.
It was generated from the per-character SVG files at immutable revision:

https://github.com/KanjiVG/kanjivg/tree/61e39cfc29724132a6f8823b166296932985a0ff/kanji

Copyright (C) Ulrich Apel.
Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 licence:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
Project: https://kanjivg.tagaini.net/

GENKŌ's derived payloads preserve each source SVG viewBox and stroke path
geometry, sort paths by KanjiVG's numbered stroke IDs, and omit SVG grouping
and annotation metadata. The manifest records the source revision and a SHA-256
hash for every packaged payload. These transformations and the packaged
stroke-order pack are made available under the same CC BY-SA 3.0 terms.

The share-alike term applies to this stroke-order data only; it does not extend
to the rest of the API or app. Any surface that renders diagrams or animations
from these payloads must show the KanjiVG credit above.

